# decompress_420: planar 4:2:0 -> packed 32-bit pixels. Each output pixel is the little-endian word
# (Y << 16) | (U << 8) | V, i.e. the BYTES in memory are  V U Y 0  (note: not U Y V X as the compressors read).
# Chroma sample (x, y/2) is shared by the 2x2 luma block. One iteration of the loop handles one chroma row
# (two luma rows) and IN_LINESIZE[0]/2 chroma samples (= IN_LINESIZE[0] pixels per row, padding included).
# Command: decompress 420 START END ILS0 ILS1 ILS2 OUT_LS OUT_ROWS PLANE0 PLANE1 PLANE2 [OFFSET]
# 4x2: Y=01..04 / 05..08, U=aa bb, V=cc dd
decompress 420 0 2 4 2 2 16 2 0102030405060708 aabb ccdd
# the output of 4x4 (two chroma rows): rows 0-1 use chroma row 0, rows 2-3 chroma row 1
decompress 420 0 4 4 2 2 16 4 0102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f10 aabb1122 ccdd3344
# extreme values: no sign extension or overflow
decompress 420 0 2 4 2 2 16 2 ff00ff00ff00ff00 ff00 00ff
# 8 luma columns, output stride exactly 4*pixels
decompress 420 0 2 8 4 4 32 2 000102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f 01020304 f1f2f3f4
